From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h618: orangepi-zero3: Add GPU OPP table

The H616 GPU node has no OPP table, so panfrost devfreq is not used and
the Mali-G31 stays at its boot clock (432 MHz).

Add the GPU OPP frequencies used by the H700 (same H616 die) Anbernic
boards, 420-648 MHz. The GPU supply is DCDC1 "vdd-gpu-sys" (810-990 mV),
which also feeds the rest of the SoC. Scaling its voltage with the GPU
(900/960 mV as on the H700 boards) made HDMI noise visible whenever the
GPU load changed, e.g. on menu transitions, so keep every OPP at 960 mV,
the voltage of the top OPP, and only scale the clock.

Experimental: under test on Orange Pi Zero3 (H618, 4 GiB).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero3.dts
@@ -11,6 +11,40 @@
 / {
 	model = "OrangePi Zero3";
 	compatible = "xunlong,orangepi-zero3", "allwinner,sun50i-h618";
+
+	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-420000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <420000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-456000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <456000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-504000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <504000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-552000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <552000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+
+		opp-648000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <648000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &ahub {
@@ -33,6 +67,7 @@
 
 &gpu {
 	mali-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 };
 
 &hdmi {
